{
  "requirement": "Model tool descriptions SHOULD NOT explain cases the model meets only\noccasionally, such as access policy, excluded or build-output paths, redaction,\npaging, and failures, and the harness SHOULD explain each of these where it\noccurs: in the tool error, or in a note in the result it affects. The model reads\nevery description on every assessment, so explaining rare cases there costs\nattention on every review for a case most never meet, and access-policy wording\nin particular can steer its reasoning away from the review. A tool whose purpose\nis one of these cases, such as `next_page`, explains it in its description.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.tool_descriptions.special_cases`.\n\n**1. Descriptions SHOULD NOT explain the rare cases.**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[descriptions_leave_paging_policy_redaction_and_failures_to_results]` runs over every tool definition, `next_page` included.\n- It asserts that no lower-cased description contains terms for each excluded case:\n  - policy and access: `policy`, `denied`, `disallow`, `habeas.toml`, `aborts`, `untracked`, `permitted`;\n  - excluded paths: `build output`, `outside the project`, `ignore rules`, `exclusion`;\n  - redaction: `redact`, `credential`;\n  - paging: `kib`, `returned in pages`;\n  - failures: `tool error`.\n- The paging terms are the narrowest part of this list. A description that said only \"results are split into pages\" would not trip them. I accept it as a reasonable proxy check.\n\n**2. The harness SHOULD explain each case where it occurs, in the tool error or in a result note.**\n- Access policy:\n  - `fn[untracked_diagnostics_name_git_add_and_an_allow_rule]` checks that the error names the path, `git add` and the `habeas.toml allow rule`.\n  - `fn[unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors]` checks the \"outside the project\" error across the tools.\n  - `src/authoring/access.rs#mod[tests]/fn[evidence_rules_are_literal_paths_not_globs]` checks that a disallowed path is refused with \"disallowed by habeas.toml rule\".\n- Excluded and build-output paths:\n  - `fn[generated_evidence_is_excluded_from_reads_search_and_discovery]` checks the \"generated evidence\" error for reads, list_files, ripgrep and ast_grep. It also covers symlinked paths.\n  - `fn[requests_for_book_or_target_output_are_ordinary_read_failures]` checks the \"holds build output … the sources it is built from are elsewhere in the project\" error for each tool, with and without `build-dir` set.\n- Redaction: `fn[only_results_with_redacted_text_carry_the_redaction_note]` checks that redacted results carry the `REDACTION_NOTE`. It also checks that results with no redaction carry none, including source or requirement text that merely contains the marker.\n- Paging:\n  - `src/authoring/pages.rs#mod[tests]/fn[large_listings_and_outlines_page_whole_entries_in_order]` is marked for this requirement. It uses the helper `fn[all_pages]`.\n  - That helper asserts that every non-final page carries `PAGE_NOTE` (\"call next_page with this page's next token\"). It also asserts that the last page has no note.\n- Failures:\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues]` covers malformed, missing, absent-item and out-of-range reads.\n  - It asserts that each failure text reaches the model in the second request and not the first.\n  - `fn[a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model]` checks that the denial names the path and the reason.\n\n**3. A tool whose purpose is a special case explains it in its description.**\n- `fn[descriptions_give_each_argument_and_the_result_form]` has `next_page` phrases that every description must contain. They include \"following page\", the list of pageable tools, \"same shape\", \"token is the page's next value\" and \"opaque\".\n- `fn[descriptions_leave_paging_policy_redaction_and_failures_to_results]` also pins the `next_page` parameter schema.\n\nNo obligation lacks a test, and no relevant test is missing its {test} marking.",
  "references": "09fa97af32a9a041637594fa3e677cc1cd11fbb6d4e5831cec4d6e2035832ab5",
